The module compiles cleanly. Signed overflow is detected when two positive operands yield a negative sum, or two negative operands yield a positive sum.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  [7:0] a,
    input  [7:0] b,
    output [7:0] s,
    output       overflow
);

    assign s = a + b;

    // Signed overflow occurs when adding two numbers with the same sign
    // produces a result with the opposite sign.
    assign overflow = (~a[7] & ~b[7] &  s[7]) |
                      ( a[7] &  b[7] & ~s[7]);

endmodule
```
